District 99 News
GLENWOOD – District 99 took home three awards at the Nebraska Educational Association’s (NEAT) conference Thursday evening inside Creighton University’s Century Ballroom.
Glenwood High School was named the “best small school,” for producing “excelling students who have achieved exemplary performance as assessed by their schools.”
“Most Outstanding Business Plan” went to Glenwood Elementary School for its Plan-4-Your-Business workshop.
And “Counselor of the Year” went to Glenn Kuehn.
Superintendent Rod Krukenberg thanked all of those recognized by recognizing a number of school personnel who helped make it happen:
The Elementary Principal’s Club, for hosting lunch for Kuehn;
All District Education Assistants for promoting one another’s accomplishments;
Jim O’Connell for being a board liaison for the conference;
District staff for taking time out of busy days;
And Glenwood Family Education for bringing out the big crowd.
